============================================================
                     QUICK MEMORY TRICKS
============================================================

FETCH  = Download only.

PULL   = Fetch + integrate.

MERGE  = Combine histories.

REBASE = Replay commits on a new base.

RESTORE = Undo working-file changes.

RESET  = Move HEAD/branch pointer.

REVERT = Create a new commit that undoes another commit.

STASH  = Temporarily hide unfinished work.

DIFF   = Compare changes.

ADD    = Stage changes.

COMMIT = Save changes to local Git history.

PUSH   = Upload commits.

CLONE  = Download repository + initialize Git.

INIT   = Turn an existing folder into a Git repository.

--cached = Work with the staging/tracking state.

--soft HEAD~1 = Undo commit, keep changes staged.

--hard HEAD~1 = Undo commit + delete changes.

--no-edit = Keep the existing commit message.

-u = Set upstream tracking.

-a = All branches.

-m = Message.

-c = Create/switch branch with switch.

-X = NOT a Git option; Maven's -X is debug mode.


